    },
    "body": "Attention still applied a floating dense `read.out` after native geometric retrieval. This adds an opt-in learned two-term signed-H4 transport bank on the actual K2 value atoms, packed four-bit dimensionless gains, and a separate i64-Q16 reducer. Each head retains its original occurrence/age/NoRead denominator; checked integer head addition precedes the remaining float model tail. The offline conditional action-learning bridge and source-bound compiler/reloader connect to the actual StackModel caller.\n\nSeven frozen-source integer cases, four new learner/admission cases and the integrated caller fixture pass. Two existing fused cases also pass. Actual saved-parent zero-update comparisons cover32 original/32 stress rows perseed: source/native choices agree128/128, all retained parent baseline logits replay, weights/null/packets stay unchanged, and answer gradients reach gains and both selectors. NaN `read.out` bypass, integer-prefix and reload checks pass. Scoped ARM64 numerical functions and same-object callees have no float/mul/div/allocator calls. Cargo fmt, claim wording and diff checks pass. One diagnostic Var-alias restore failure is preserved and repaired with independent F32 snapshot bytes.\n\nThe untrained banks score7/5 and0/4 versus parents24/22 and32/32. This is construction, not a learned-quality result or family retirement. K2 transports cannot represent arbitrary donor blocks; offline broader weight compilation remains retained. Wide producer coefficients, the float trunk/vocabulary output, bounded access and whole-language/energy qualification remain open. Next is bank-only answer learning with an actual B8 cost check before dose admission.\n\nReferences #1512. References #973.\n",
