      "body": "# Independent exact-head delivery review — geometric read composition\n\n**APPROVED for protected delivery at exact head `918bd80ace3c54a08631ca091ed475aa19083469`**, relative to base `4e10dc1a936a926e1e2a4f096d749473fb87d95a`. No material unresolved source, arithmetic, evidence-binding or claim-scope blocker found. This approval covers the connected attention value-to-residual composition implementation and its zero-update construction evidence. It does not promote learned quality, geometric superiority, general donor conversion, full native attention, whole-model serving or energy.\n\nReviewer: principal mathematician, non-author. October2,2026. No Cargo, model run, optimization, Git mutation or implementation edit was performed for this review. The worktree was clean when checked. The commit contains exactly13 intended paths: nine Rust source/registration files and four evidence/state/plan documents.\n\nThe review reuses the completed static mathematical review, compiler/binding review, repaired-diagnostic review and independently audited sealed construction outputs. It does not require a repeated model campaign.\n\n## Exact binding checks\n\n- Each of the nine `source_sha256` fields in the committed evidence receipt equals both the exact Git blob contents and the current frozen source bytes.\n- The committed `construction_reports` objects exactly equal the two actual saved reports; all ten embedded execution records exactly equal their retained execution JSON files. The embedded instruction audit equals its retained JSON.\n- The successful construction binary is `3ba67ff1abab085fa4df8b636f3a896ea9ffc223a073d6b8e619021f9db27d59`; I separately checked its current bytes. The repaired example is `c9c992ad8f53b5dc363327b3830d725eaa209b363727d6dc46a398759c6a7465`. Earlier Cargo receipt executable fields are not used as claims about the test binary; source hashes and actual named test logs establish their scoped execution.\n- Receipt SHA256: `28248420cff0d5ddcc40e59a52f5ae9ab37f9d082e622b64f6e1fe8a6c7692cd`. Cumulative charge arithmetic is internally consistent; elapsed wrapper/model measurements and the cost-cutoff scope are distinguished.\n- Both successful17-file manifests and the preserved failed14-file manifest were independently verified by exact inventory, length and BLAKE3 content. Parent report/panel/episode/logit joins and256 saved query-head weight/denominator joins were independently checked in the result audit.\n\n## What the evidence establishes\n\nSeven integer tests, four new learner/admission checks, two incidentally selected existing tests, and the extended actual StackModel fixture pass:14 distinct cases, of which12 directly exercise this change. The repaired construction runs each cover32 original plus32 stress records. All128 source/native answer choices agree. Ordinary answer CE has finite positive gradients to gains and both selector families on one actual-parent example per seed. Native packets, scores/age/NoRead weights and per-head denominator ordering are preserved by executed checks. Exact integer causal-prefix, independently reloaded source/native artifacts and poisoned dense `read.out` bypass checks pass.\n\nThe initialized bank gives16/128 correct versus110/128 with the retained legacy map:2 gains,96 losses and108 changed predictions. The maximum observed source/native answer-logit difference is0.0002684593200683594. These values are correctly reported as zero-update construction observations, with real-softmax/F32 source versus integer-LUT/Q16 reduction included in the difference. There is no donor-reconstruction or answer-quality admission gate. The initial Var-alias restoration failure is preserved and accurately scoped as a diagnostic defect; the independent F32 snapshot repair changes no model arithmetic.\n\nThe scoped ARM64 audit covers9 same-object bodies/1167 instructions, with no banned arithmetic or allocator calls in that scope; external memory and bounds/length failure helpers remain explicit. It is not final-linked/external-helper or whole-model certification. The wide Q16 payload and per-head i128 normalization bounds match the actual implementation, with the legacy i32 reader artifact unchanged.\n\n## Documentation and next action\n\nI read the exact committed integration report, current-state entry and project-track delta. They preserve the K2 operator restriction, fixed q4 gain scale, selector identities, earlier wide-coefficient limitations, float trunk/vocabulary tail, and distinction between signed geometric actions and an arbitrary dense compiler. The next action is bank-only ordinary-answer learning, preceded by the actual B8 zero-update cost check and a prospective fixed-dose card. No fit has run at this committed checkpoint. That is a justified next question; untrained losses neither promote nor retire the family. The final vocabulary head and the concurrent dialogue/session track are unchanged.\n\n## Reviewed Git blobs\n\n| Path | Git blob |\n|---|---|\n| `crates/uor-r4-integer/src/geometric_composed_read.rs` | `65a0c79cc20cf75cb78324bbed083a4b52daa8d9` |\n| `crates/uor-r4-integer/src/geometric_composition.rs` | `77026165a198ccab0f5533f987205b2410ad079f` |\n| `crates/uor-r4-integer/src/lib.rs` | `4a463f6d58a83ff7b54986ef1d12d508162f5174` |\n| `crates/uor-r4-training/examples/attention-geometric-composition.rs` | `36bfcd367ba6ed3bceaaf056401aef5e5a899392` |\n| `crates/uor-r4-training/src/geometric_composition.rs` | `32f8d77772abb46214266d61306550ee25971c1b` |\n| `crates/uor-r4-training/src/geometric_composition_native.rs` | `133710138b7d77dfe2b8fa248cbd605466d97e46` |\n| `crates/uor-r4-training/src/geometric_read_native.rs` | `124c0b7c755196a750ed6015ba9b3c8f902b3c7a` |\n| `crates/uor-r4-training/src/geometric_stack.rs` | `baef3dee22bc2f0eef2974e84e1a9fc0c8dac411` |\n| `crates/uor-r4-training/src/lib.rs` | `df561363f7df8b4942956729696a903e1a57c032` |\n| `docs/evidence/geometric-read-composition-2026-10-02.json` | `782571b59169527d3a5214563d257199b31f2191` |\n| `docs/integration/current-state.md` | `02ef4529018e82a0ba5adeb2d0c833164e1cd186` |\n| `docs/integration/geometric-read-composition-2026-10-02.md` | `4fb93d10bad9ffc8e23a650aead67cd77196ffb7` |\n| `docs/integration/project-track.md` | `900b316135035cb51befe0ddbb176e4c202f640f` |\n\nRetained independent notes:\n\n- `implementation-math-review.md`: `1dff92d1dffb2b4b30a2d85ab31284a94c204cefd938ea911f3a68e8fcb949aa`.\n- `construction-result-review.md`: `1435ba45b7e0a78d866c8ce3c03aa3e493257fb83ad6145c2af63aa93eeb43de`.\n\nThe earlier implementation note deliberately retains its then-pending execution status; this exact-head review supplies the later completed-evidence disposition without rewriting history.\n",
